## Decisions not in the plan

- The error line reads e.g. `line 2: expected 2 fields, got 1\n` (code 1). The plan only required "one line naming the 1-based line number," so I included the expected/got counts for clarity — easy to simplify if you want just the line number.
- I placed `--json` last in the check order, matching the existing `--upper` → `--count` pattern. Note that `--count` still counts raw non-empty newline-split lines, untouched as requested.

